---
import { rich } from '../lib/rich.mjs';
import { bars, clusters } from '../lib/viz.mjs';
import jet from '../data/jetson.json';
import Foresight from './figures/Foresight.astro';

const r = rich;
const GH = 'https://github.com/harshithkantamneni/';
const RESUME = '/resume/inference/Harshith_Kantamneni_Resume.pdf';

// Cells from the manuscript's grid table: [experts on GPU, stock, FreeToken, cache]
const GRID = {
  Bgpt: [['11%', 34.9, 54.0, 69.9], ['25%', 40.0, 85.6, 109.2], ['40%', 47.7, 132.2, 152.5]],
  Bqwen: [['12.5%', 19.5, 38.7, 40.0], ['25%', 22.1, 54.7, 63.1], ['43.75%', 28.4, 103.1, 108.2]],
  Sgpt: [['11%', 28.9, 48.0, 57.9], ['25%', 33.6, 78.7, 94.1], ['40%', 40.1, 122.2, 133.6]],
  Sqwen: [['12.5%', 16.1, 32.7, 33.5], ['25%', 18.5, 51.4, 53.9], ['43.75%', 23.8, 98.3, 95.8]],
};
const decMax = Math.max(...jet.decode.map((d) => d.us));
const { as = 'h2' } = Astro.props;
const Top = as, Sub = as === 'h1' ? 'h2' : 'h3', Also = as === 'h1' ? 'h3' : 'h4';
---
<section class="opener i" id="inference" data-chapter="i" data-resume={RESUME}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Top>Inference</Top>
    <p>One layer up: a real model, and how long the next token takes.</p>
    <div class="ol">
      <a href="#seconds">Where the seconds go</a>
      <a href="#cache">What the cache bought</a>
      <a href="#edge">The same question at 15 W</a>
      {as === 'h1' ? <a href="/">See the whole stack</a> : <a href="/inference/">Only the inference work</a>}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="i" data-chapter="i" data-resume={RESUME}>
  <section class="scene" id="seconds" data-scene>
    <div class="wrap">
      <Sub class="scene-t">Where the seconds go when the model doesn't fit</Sub>
      <div class="scene-g">
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step" data-step="0" data-run="fs:000"><p set:html={r('gpt-oss-120b needs [[wsg.size|about 61 GB]] and the card has [[wsg.size|32 GB]], so most experts wait in host memory and each token stalls on reads. I built an expert cache in llama.cpp for this, for batch-1 decode.')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="1" data-run="fs:110"><p set:html={r('How close is that to the best possible? I computed a limit and added oracles to the engine, with its copy table on. An oracle\'s cache schedule barely moves it alone, and neither does reading each expert once, but together they reach [[wsg.breakdown|15.13]] ms. Flip the switches yourself.')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="2" data-run="fs:111"><p set:html={r('On this machine, [[wsg.breakdown|36%]] of the gap stayed even after all three, and [[wsg.gap|43-52%]] averaged over three groups of machines. Four policies without foresight got [[wsg.online|at most 6%]] of what the read-ahead oracle gained, on [[wsg.online|5 fast-link machines]].')} /></div>
          <div class="scene-links">
            <a href="/work/where-the-seconds-go/">Read the case study</a>
            <a href={GH + 'moe-speed-of-light'}>See the code and data</a>
            <a href={GH + 'moe-speed-of-light/blob/main/paper/ieee-paper.pdf'}>Read the manuscript, not peer reviewed</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage">
          <div class="frames">
            <Foresight f="0,1,2" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scene" id="cache" data-scene>
    <div class="wrap">
      <Sub class="scene-t">What the cache bought</Sub>
      <div class="scene-g">
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step" data-step="0" data-run="grid:Bgpt"><p set:html={r('Faster than FreeToken in [[sec.vs_ft|11 of 12]] configurations, and [[wsg.grid|2.0-4.0×]] stock llama.cpp in all of them. On a separate rental with FreeToken tuned, across six cells, the ratio is [[wsg.ft_tuned|0.98-1.17×]].')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="1" data-run="grid:Sqwen"><p set:html={r('The one slower cell is [[wsg.slower|0.97×]], at the largest Qwen3 budget on the stock-clock host. On that host, swapping my admission rule for LRU ran [[wsg.lru|6-21%]] slower, so I read most of the difference as that rule. This is batch 1 only, and stock is a weak baseline.')} /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage">
          <div class="frames">
            <figure class="frame key" data-f="0,1" id="gridx">
              <figcaption>Tokens per second at batch 1, on 2 RTX 5090 hosts. Pick a host and a model.</figcaption>
              <div class="seg" data-k="host" role="group" aria-label="Host" style="margin-top:12px">
                <button type="button" data-v="B" aria-pressed="true">Faster-memory host</button>
                <button type="button" data-v="S" aria-pressed="false">Stock-clock host</button>
              </div>
              <div class="seg" data-k="model" role="group" aria-label="Model">
                <button type="button" data-v="gpt" aria-pressed="true">gpt-oss-120b</button>
                <button type="button" data-v="qwen" aria-pressed="false">Qwen3-30B-A3B</button>
              </div>
              <div class="legend"><span><i></i>My cache</span><span><i class="mid"></i>FreeToken</span><span><i class="dim"></i>Stock llama.cpp</span></div>
              {Object.entries(GRID).map(([k, rows]) => (
                <div data-combo={k} set:html={clusters(rows.map(([gpu, stock, ft, c]) => ({
                  label: gpu, note: 'on the GPU',
                  bars: [
                    { value: c, text: c.toFixed(1) },
                    { value: ft, text: ft.toFixed(1), tone: 'mid' },
                    { value: stock, text: stock.toFixed(1), tone: 'dim' },
                  ],
                })), { max: 155 })} />
              ))}
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scene" id="edge" data-scene>
    <div class="wrap">
      <Sub class="scene-t">The same question at 15 watts</Sub>
      <div class="scene-g">
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step" data-step="0"><p set:html={r('I profiled attention and KV-cache decode with Nsight on a [[jet.power|15 W]] edge board. Decode holds steady up to [[jet.decode|1024]], then climbs.')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="1"><p set:html={r('Fused attention ran [[jet.fused|2.78-5.55×]] faster than a manual matmul and softmax baseline, which is a low bar. It\'s one sweep of kernels, not a model.')} /></div>
          <div class="scene-links">
            <a href={GH + 'edge-llm-gpu-profiling'}>See the code and raw data</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage">
          <div class="frames">
            <figure class="frame key" data-f="0,1">
              <figcaption>KV-cache decode on a Jetson Orin Nano, single stream, microseconds per token, by context length</figcaption>
              <p class="f-read" set:html={r('[[jet.decode|398.1]]<small> microseconds</small>')} />
              <p class="f-sub" set:html={r('at [[jet.decode|8192]], from [[jet.decode|63.1]] at [[jet.decode|256]]')} />
              <Fragment set:html={bars(jet.decode.map((d) => ({ label: String(d.S), value: d.us, text: d.us.toFixed(1) })), { max: decMax })} />
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scene also">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="alsos">
        <div>
          <Also class="at"><a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/46295#issuecomment-5788867616">vLLM RFC #46295</a></Also>
          <p set:html={r('A measurement comment on someone else\'s RFC. On [[rfc.oracle|one H200]], a per-workload oracle improved on the best static table by [[rfc.oracle|at most 1.8%]], and vLLM\'s MFU byte model overcounted reads [[rfc.mfu|up to 3×]] in the worst cell.')} />
          <p class="st">Comment, offline and synthetic</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <Also class="at"><a href={GH + 'llm-inference-benchmarking'}>vLLM serving benchmark</a></Also>
          <p set:html={r('Load-tested vLLM on H100 NVL. TPOT ran [[srv.graphs|31-34%]] lower with CUDA graphs, and FP8 cut it [[srv.fp8|27-36%]]. [[srv.runs|One run per rate]], so it\'s a first pass.')} />
          <p class="st">Public repo</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
